The antioxidant activity was measured by the extinction of the absorption peak at 517 nm, after the reaction between 100 µL of the extract and 2.90 mL of a DPPH (100 µM) ethanolic solution. The samples were incubated in a water bath (Kacil, model BM-02, Brazil) at 25 °C, in the dark, for 30 min. The DPPH solution was previously diluted in ethanol until it reached an absorbance between 0.900 and 1.000. Trolox was used as the standard for constructing the analytical curve. The results were expressed as percentage of inhibition, as per Eq.  5 . 5 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
